% The customs background (lpsPlus docs/strategy/FactsBackground.md §6.1):
% the kinds of plastics articles and the forms of plastics, in the words of
% the tariff. Each word is a name that the tariff's Chapter 39 (its headings
% and its notes 6, 8, 10 and 11) or a US Customs ruling gives to a kind of
% good that the rules of Chapter 39 read. Bridges.
%
% Left out, because they name a legal category and not a thing a seller
% names: part, waste, scrap, parings, structural element, building fitting.
%
% Used only to read facts from a text (language reference §14.5).

the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.

the templates are:
    *a thing* is called *a name*; undefined.
    the field *a field* of *a thing* reads *a value*; undefined.
    *a name* is a word for the kind *a kind*.
    *a field* is a field that names the kind.
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.

the knowledge base articles background includes:

HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39 is published at "https://hts.usitc.gov/reststop/file?release=currentRelease&filename=Chapter%2039".
the text of HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39 is at "sources/hts/chapter_39.txt".
the listing format is published at "https://huggingface.co/datasets/ATH-MaaS/HSCodeComp".
the text of the listing format is at "sources/listings/marketplace_fields.txt".
ruling NY N318445 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N318445".
the text of ruling NY N318445 is at "sources/cbp/N318445.txt".
ruling NY N330412 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N330412".
the text of ruling NY N330412 is at "sources/cbp/N330412.txt".
