rule kind_by_name with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "PLASTICS AND ARTICLES THEREOF":
the kind of a good is a kind
    if the good is called a name
    and the name is a word for the kind the kind.

rule kind_by_field with provenance the listing format,
        confer "Item Type (64 listings): the kind of product in the seller's words":
the kind of a good is a kind
    if the field a field of the good reads a value
    and the field is a field that names the kind
    and the value is a word for the kind the kind.

scenario hose is:
    hose is called "garden hose".
    seat is called "toilet seat".
    resin is called "pellets".
    the field "item type" of wrap reads "film".
    the field "type" of shade one reads "roller shade".
    kinds expects answers ["the kind of hose is hose", "the kind of seat is lavatory seat", "the kind of resin is pellets", "the kind of wrap is film", "the kind of shade one is shade"].

query kinds is:
    the kind of which good is which kind.
